WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:11.480
Last time: grids · across first, then up

3
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:18.660
Chapter 3 · Symmetry and Patterns

4
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:26.300
Fold · Mirror · Pattern

5
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.200
Meet Riya, making a Diwali rangoli

6
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:43.680
"Draw the other wing. Make it match!"

7
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:51.690
How can Riya check? Think!

8
00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:58.620
Nani's trick: fold it down the middle

9
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:07.550
Both halves match exactly!

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.510
That fold line is a LINE OF SYMMETRY

11
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.780
A fold line where both halves match exactly

12
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:24.110
It works just like a mirror

13
00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:30.990
Symmetrical: has at least one fold line

14
00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:43.260
Not every line works! Halves must match

15
00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:55.970
House: fold down the middle → it matches!

16
00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:08.100
A or F: which one folds and matches?

17
00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:24.770
A matches! F, G and R don't

18
00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:29.660
Some shapes have more than one!

19
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:48.820
Square: 4 lines of symmetry

20
00:02:48.820 --> 00:03:03.330
Rectangle: up-down and across

21
00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:17.280
Corner to corner? No match! Only 2 lines

22
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:27.380
The fold line works like a mirror

23
00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:38.980
2 left of the fold → 2 right of the fold

24
00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:49.690
3 squares left → where's its partner?

25
00:03:49.690 --> 00:04:00.510
3 squares right! Same distance, other side

26
00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:06.640
The rangoli border is a pattern

27
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:15.320
Pattern unit: the small part that repeats

28
00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:25.510
Red, blue, red, blue, red → blue!

29
00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:38.620
Star, dot, dot, star, dot, dot, star, ?, ?

30
00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:47.040
Dot, dot! The unit is star, dot, dot

31
00:04:47.040 --> 00:05:01.880
Square, triangle, triangle… what's tile 10?

32
00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:11.130
Unit: square, triangle, triangle (3 tiles)

33
00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:21.770
Tiles 1, 4, 7, 10 are squares → square!

34
00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:30.070
Game art repeats one small tile

35
00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:33.770
Your turn: practice check

36
00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:44.420
Does a heart have a line of symmetry?

37
00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:55.950
Yes! One line, top dip to bottom point

38
00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:02.310
Symmetry = fold, and both halves match

39
00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:07.100
Square: 4 lines · Rectangle: 2 lines

40
00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.950
Missing half: same distance, other side

41
00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:16.200
Find the repeating unit

42
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:22.450
Chapter 3 done!

43
00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:29.250
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
